2. Network Devices and Their Functions
Router
A router connects the local network to the Internet and forwards data packets between networks.
Switch
A switch connects multiple devices within the LAN and allows communication between them.
Access Point
An access point provides wireless connectivity to devices using Wi-Fi.
Computer/Laptop
These are end-user devices used to access network resources.
Printer
A network printer allows multiple users to print documents through the LAN.
