6. Observations
Difference Between Wired and Wireless Network
Wired connections provide higher speed and stability.
Wireless connections provide mobility and convenience.
Wired networks are less affected by interference.
Wireless networks may experience signal loss and speed variations.
Role of Subnet Mask
Subnet mask divides an IP address into network and host portions.
It helps identify whether a device belongs to the same network or a different network.
It improves network management and communication.
Conclusion
This experiment was conducted to study LAN topology, networking devices, connection types, network speed, and address configuration. A star topology was observed, and the functions of various network devices were studied. The network parameters such as MAC Address, IPv4 Address, and Subnet Mask were obtained using networking commands. The experiment helped in understanding the basic concepts of computer networking and LAN communication.